@startuml GitEasyTrustBoundary
title GitEasy - Security / Trust-Boundary View (v1.5.5)
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

package "Untrusted inputs" {
  component "User-supplied remote URL\n(Set-Token, Set-Ssh)" <<boundary>> as UserUrl
  component ".git/config read path\n(Get-GERemoteUrl)" <<boundary>> as GitConfig
  component "git credential layer output\n(Reset-Login stdout/stderr)" <<boundary>> as CredOut
  component "git error messages\n(may quote the remote URL)" <<boundary>> as GitErr
  component "In-progress operation state\n(.git/MERGE_HEAD etc.)" <<boundary>> as GitState
}

package "Security guards" {
  component "Test-GERemoteUrlSafe\n[F-01, F-04]\nreject URLs with embedded user:token@" <<helper>> as G1
  component "Format-GESafeUrl\n[F-01, F-05, F-06]\nstrip userinfo@ from URL-shaped text" <<helper>> as G2
  component "Format-GESafeLogLine\n[F-02, F-03]\nredact password=/token= lines" <<helper>> as G3
  component "Assert-GESafeSave\n[state guard]\nreject when merge/rebase/conflict active" <<helper>> as G4
}

package "Safe zone" {
  component "Invoke-GEGit" <<helper>> as Engine
  component "Log session helpers\n(Start / Add / Complete)" <<helper>> as LogH
  database "Diagnostic log files\n(plaintext on disk)" <<store>> as Logs
}

UserUrl --> G1 : input gate;\nSet-Token + Set-Ssh call this\nbefore writing to git remote
GitConfig --> G2 : read-path gate;\nGet-GERemoteUrl output sanitised\nbefore display or log
CredOut --> G3 : output sanitiser;\nReset-Login captures cred-layer output\nand passes through this first
GitErr --> G2 : error message sanitiser;\nTest-Login sanitises ls-remote errors\nbefore returning them [F-05]
GitState --> G4 : state guard;\nchecks MERGE_HEAD, CHERRY_PICK_HEAD,\nREVERT_HEAD, BISECT_START,\nrebase-merge, rebase-apply

G1 --> Engine : validated URL only
G2 --> LogH : sanitised text
G3 --> LogH : sanitised credential output
G4 --> Engine : guard passes, git call proceeds

Engine --> G2 : [F-06] sanitise each ArgumentList\nelement before log step and throw
LogH --> Logs : write

note bottom of G4
  Checked by every mutating command\n(Save-Work, Undo-Changes, New-WorkBranch,\nSwitch-Work, Clear-Junk, New-Release,\nRestore-File) before any git call.
end note
@enduml
